# Strahd's coffin (K86), the prop cat_strahds_coffin in castle_ravenloft_catacombs_strahd
# (docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_catacombs.md §5). ADR 0014: Strahd is destroyed only here.
# empty: night, never beaten, he is out. asleep: day, never beaten; the stake wakes him (cat_daylight_waking), and
# beaten he mists into the coffin (strahd_in_coffin, the engine). resting: strahd_in_coffin; the keepers' fight has
# already happened on entering the tomb. the_end sets strahd_destroyed, moves strahds_lair and ends the game.
# vladimir: the pact sworn at Argynvostholt (vladimir_pact) brings him down the stair to stop the killing blow.

~ coffin
if flag.strahd_destroyed
-> ashes
endif
if flag.strahd_in_coffin
-> resting
endif
if day
-> asleep
endif
-> empty

~ ashes
Narrator: The coffin holds a long drift of grey ash in the shape of a man, and a stake standing upright in it.
end_game

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- He is out

~ empty
Narrator: The coffin is empty. A bed of dark earth lies in it, pressed into the shape of a tall man, and cold.
Narrator: He is out. Somewhere far above you it is night, and the night is his.
if treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_strahds_tomb
interject tag:curious: Nobody guards an empty bed this hard unless something else in the room matters. That chest, for one.
endif
* [if item:holy_water and not flag.cat_coffin_hallowed] Pour holy water into his earth. -> hallow
* Close the lid and leave it. -> END

~ hallow
take holy_water 1
set cat_coffin_hallowed
Narrator: The water goes into the earth with a hiss like a cat, a curl of steam and a smell of struck matches. The earth will remember.
interject class:cleric: It won't keep him from coming home. It will make sure he hates the bed when he gets here.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- He sleeps by day

~ asleep
Narrator: He is here. He lies in the coffin with his hands folded on his chest, as neat as a body laid out by good servants. His eyes are shut. He does not breathe; he has never needed to.
if guest:ireena
interject guest:ireena: Don't talk. Don't wake him. Just do it.
endif
interject tag:blunt: He's asleep. We won't get a better chance than this.
interject class:wizard: Unless he isn't asleep. Unless he's lying still to see what we'll do.
* Drive the stake into his heart while he sleeps. -> wake
* [if item:sunsword] Draw the Sunsword over him. -> wake_sun
* Back away and let him sleep. -> END

~ wake
Narrator: The point touches his shirt, and his eyes are open. He was never as deep asleep as that.
Strahd: In my own bedroom, at this hour. You might at least have knocked.
combat cat_daylight_waking

~ wake_sun
Narrator: The blade wakes in your hand, and so does he: the light finds his face and his eyes snap open, burning.
Strahd [angry]: My brother's sword. I threw that sword as far as a man can throw anything.
combat cat_daylight_waking

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- He rests, beaten

~ resting
if flag.vladimir_pact and not flag.vladimir_pact_broken and not flag.cat_vladimir_stood_aside
-> vladimir
endif
Narrator: The mist has gone back into him. He lies in the coffin grey and still, and only his eyes move. They are perfectly clear.
if flag.cat_coffin_hallowed
Narrator: The earth you blessed smokes under him. He came home to a bed that burns and lay down in it anyway, because there was nowhere else to go.
endif
Strahd: Well. Here we are. I confess I had imagined this room with more candles.
if guest:ireena
Strahd: Ireena. You came all the way down. You always did come, in the end.
interject guest:ireena: Not for you. Never once for you.
endif
-> resting_menu

~ resting_menu
* Drive the stake through his heart. -> stake
* [if guest:ireena] Give Ireena the stake. -> ireena_stake
* [if item:sunsword] End it with the Sunsword's light. -> sunsword
* [if item:holy_symbol_of_ravenkind] Raise the Holy Symbol and call up the dawn. -> symbol
* [if not flag.cat_last_words_heard] Let him speak. -> last_words
* Not yet. Close the lid. -> not_yet

~ last_words
set cat_last_words_heard
Strahd: You will find the valley very quiet without me. Very small. You will go home, and nothing there will ever be as large as I was.
Strahd: Close the lid. Walk away. Come back in a hundred years and we will do this again. It will be the most interesting thing that ever happens to any of you.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: You're not large. You're loud. Sir Pellam was large. No.
interject name:thistle: Home's the whole Thornwood. You're a box in a cellar. No.
interject class:rogue: He's stalling. Every word is another minute for him to mend.
-> resting_menu

~ not_yet
Narrator: The lid comes down over his eyes. They stay open the whole way. He will not lie here for ever.
-> END

~ stake
set cat_staked_by = "party"
Narrator: You set the point over his heart and lean on it with all your weight. For a moment the wood will not go in. Then it does.
-> the_end

~ ireena_stake
set cat_staked_by = "ireena"
Ireena: Give it here.
Narrator: She takes the stake in both hands and kneels on the edge of the coffin.
Strahd: Tatyana.
Ireena: No.
Narrator: She doesn't say anything else. She doesn't need to.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +2 thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +2 liriel_dawnsong +1: You gave Ireena the stake
-> the_end

~ sunsword
set cat_staked_by = "sun"
Narrator: The blade blazes up like a shutter thrown open on a summer noon, and the light falls straight down into the coffin.
Strahd: Ah. There it is. I had forgotten what it looked like.
-> the_end

~ symbol
set cat_staked_by = "sun"
Narrator: The silver raven flares in your fist, and the tomb fills with morning, real morning, the first this room has ever held.
-> the_end

~ the_end
set strahd_destroyed
quest strahds_lair destroyed
Narrator: He comes apart the way old paper does in a fire: all at once, quietly, edges first. What is left in the coffin is ash, and a smell of dust and cold iron.
if flag.cat_staked_by == "ireena"
Narrator: Ireena stays on her knees a long moment. Then she stands, and wipes her hands on her skirt, and doesn't look back at it.
endif
if flag.cat_ireena_at_tomb == "promised"
interject guest:ireena: Sergei. I promised him. When we're out of here, there's a pool I have to go back to.
elif flag.cat_ireena_at_tomb == "farewell"
interject guest:ireena: It's done. It's actually done. I'm going to sleep with the window open.
endif
if flag.cat_oathbreakers_beaten
Narrator: Vladimir Horngaard lies at the foot of the stair where he fell. For the first time in four hundred years his face is not angry.
elif flag.cat_vladimir_stood_aside
Narrator: At the foot of the stair Vladimir Horngaard lowers his head, and his knights behind him do the same.
elif flag.order_fate == "ride"
Narrator: On the black stair the dead knights of the Order raise their swords together in salute.
endif
interject class:cleric: Morninglord. If you're still up there somewhere, look at this.
Narrator: Far above you, through all the stone of the castle, something lets go, like a breath held for four hundred years.
end_game

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Vladimir's pact

~ vladimir
Narrator: Armour on the black stair. Vladimir Horngaard comes down into the tomb with his knights at his back and stops at the foot of the dais.
Vladimir Horngaard: You swore an oath at my table. Break him. Do not end him.
Vladimir Horngaard: Death is a door for him. I will not hold it open.
* [if flag.vladimir_last_words_known] The dragon told you to let them go home, Vladimir. Let them go. -> vladimir_released
* [Persuasion DC 18] He has had four hundred years of punishment, and it has made him worse. End it with us. -> vladimir_moved | vladimir_unmoved
* We break our oath. Stand aside or fall. -> vladimir_fight
* Not yet. (Close the lid.) -> not_yet

~ vladimir_released
set cat_vladimir_stood_aside
Narrator: For a long time Vladimir says nothing at all.
Vladimir Horngaard: Let them go home. He said it with his last breath, and I took them to war instead.
Vladimir Horngaard: Do it, then. And afterwards I will take my knights home.
Narrator: He steps back from the dais, and his knights step back with him.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +3 liriel_dawnsong +1: You reminded Vladimir of the dragon's last words at Strahd's coffin
-> resting

~ vladimir_moved
set cat_vladimir_stood_aside
Vladimir Horngaard: Worse. Yes. So am I.
Narrator: He steps back from the dais, and his knights step back with him.
-> resting

~ vladimir_unmoved
set vladimir_pact_broken
Vladimir Horngaard: Words. I have heard four hundred years of words. Draw.
combat cat_oathbreakers

~ vladimir_fight
set vladimir_pact_broken
Vladimir Horngaard: Then you are what he is. Oathbreakers.
approve godrick_pendlebrook -1: You broke your oath to Vladimir at Strahd's coffin
combat cat_oathbreakers
